# Normalize line endings: store everything as LF in the repo. Git will convert
# to the platform default on checkout (CRLF on Windows, LF elsewhere) while the
# committed blobs stay LF. This keeps source, shell scripts, and configs correct
# on every OS and lets editors always detect UTF-8 without CRLF ambiguity.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that are always binary (never touch line endings).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.eot binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.wasm binary
*.ico binary
